  "Sanctum|INF multi-LST pool": {
    "audit_security": { why: "Sanctum Infinity has been reviewed through three independent audits, with additional audit coverage for its reserve pool. Its custom codebase is also publicly available.", held: "We attempted to verify that the deployed program matches the published source code, but the resulting hashes did not match. Because of that, we cannot currently confirm that the exact code running on-chain is the same code covered by the audits." },
    "maturity": { why: "Infinity has operated since early 2024 and held about $156.3M at the time of our review. It is also part of Sanctum’s broader liquid-staking infrastructure, which supported about $1.33B in assets.", held: "Infinity has only about 2.5 years of operating history, which is relatively short for a product with several interacting components. The exact deployed program version was also only about four months old." },
    "upgrade_admin_authority": { why: "Sanctum documents an 11-member committee requiring 6 approvals for important program changes, and the same structure is referenced across both Sanctum and Jupiter documentation.", held: "We could not independently verify that 6-of-11 control structure on-chain. The same upgrade authority also appears to control multiple Sanctum programs, concentrating administrative power across the broader Sanctum stack." },
    "manager_discretion": { why: "Sanctum cannot directly seize users’ INF holdings, and users can permissionlessly exchange INF for assets held by the basket.", held: "Sanctum decides which liquid staking tokens can be included in Infinity, how the basket is composed, and certain pricing and fee parameters. INF holders cannot individually veto changes to the assets backing the basket." },
    "strategy_complexity": { why: "Infinity’s structure and components are visible and can be examined individually.", held: "The system is complex. It combines a custom controller, separate on-chain pricing programs for individual liquid staking tokens, fee modules, a reserve pool, and a basket containing many different assets. Each additional component creates another place where an error could affect the product." },
    "composability_dependency": { why: "Holding several liquid staking tokens reduces dependence on any single token or staking provider.", held: "INF is ultimately backed by tokens issued by other staking protocols, so it inherits their risks. If a component liquid staking token suffers a program failure or loses value relative to SOL, that can directly affect the Infinity basket." },
    "oracle_risk": { why: "Infinity does not rely on external price feeds to value the liquid staking tokens it holds. Each component is valued using information from its own on-chain staking state.", held: "Those values are calculated through Sanctum’s own custom pricing programs. They are on-chain and transparent, but they add another custom code layer whose correctness the basket depends on." },
    "liquidity_withdrawal": { why: "Users can exchange INF directly for liquid staking tokens held by the basket without a fixed waiting period or operator approval.", held: "That does not necessarily provide an immediate exit into SOL. Users may receive another liquid staking token that has its own liquidity limitations or requires waiting through the normal unstaking process. In our tests, a 10,000 INF exit remained close to underlying value, while a 50,000 INF exit found no viable market route to SOL." },
    "asset_stablecoin_risk": { why: "Infinity is diversified across multiple liquid staking tokens backed by natively staked SOL. It does not introduce stablecoin exposure or the impermanent-loss risk of a two-asset liquidity pool.", held: "Every component can still trade above or below the value of its underlying SOL. A significant discount in one of the basket’s larger holdings can therefore reduce the value of INF as a whole." },
    "withdrawal_fee_transparency": { why: "We found no contradiction between Sanctum’s published fee information and the fee behavior we observed elsewhere in its products.", held: "Infinity’s fees can vary by swap and configuration. We did not independently decode the live fee parameters of the Infinity pool during this review." },
    "operational_dependency_risk": { why: "Sanctum operates substantial liquid-staking infrastructure across Solana, and we found no major adverse operational event involving Infinity during our review.", held: "Important functions such as selecting supported liquid staking tokens, maintaining pricing modules, and managing the basket depend on Sanctum. We found only limited public detail about the internal operational controls behind these processes." },
    "incident_history": { why: "We found no publicly documented exploit, user-fund loss event, or major litigation involving Infinity or Sanctum’s core infrastructure during roughly 2.5 years of operation.", held: "This reflects the public information we could find at the time of review, not a formal or exhaustive incident-history report. We therefore do not treat the absence of discovered incidents as proof of a completely clean record." },
  },
  // HAND-AUTHORED, PRODUCT-OWNER-APPROVED user-facing copy (2026-08-11).
